{
  "_README": [
    "THE DETERMINISM PIN FOR CanonicalStateWriter (14 section 16.6).",
    "",
    "*** CHANGING A ROW IN THIS FILE IS A DETERMINISM BREAK, NEVER A TEST FIX. ***",
    "",
    "Every row is a committed (value -> canonical bytes -> hash) fact. If a row starts",
    "failing, the implementation changed, not the expectation: every stateHash ever",
    "issued to a client just moved, every client mirror stops agreeing with the server,",
    "every battle LogHash stops reproducing, and the parity and reconnect chaos tests",
    "(14 section 13) start comparing fiction. Fix the code.",
    "",
    "The only legitimate edit is ADDING rows. If a row must genuinely change, that is a",
    "deliberate, announced break: it needs its own commit, a SchemaVersion bump with a",
    "versioned migration (14 section 16.6), a note in the decision log, and a story for",
    "every persisted stateHash.",
    "",
    "These rows are asserted byte-identical on every target platform -- Linux x64",
    "(server), Android ARM64 and iOS ARM64 -- by the cross-platform determinism job",
    "(14 section 8.2, task M5-12), alongside Rng/Hash64ReferenceVectors.json. They are",
    "embedded in the SlayIdleRepeat.Core.Tests assembly so that job finds them",
    "regardless of working directory.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE. These rows were NOT generated from SlayIdleRepeat.Core. They were",
    "generated by an independent Python transcription of the 14 section 16.6",
    "specification table, whose FNV-1a 64 first reproduced all 29 published vectors",
    "below. SlayIdleRepeat.Core then had to match it."
  ],
